# KnowledgeOS Overview

Personal AI knowledge vault: URL → Hangfire ingestion → OpenRouter AI score → Inbox → Vault.

## Stack & paths

- **Backend**: `KnowledgeOS.Backend/` — .NET 10, EF Core + PostgreSQL (TPT), Identity + JWT, Hangfire
- **Frontend**: `knowledgeos-frontend/` — Next.js 16, React 19, Tailwind 4
- **Run**: `docker compose up -d --build` from repo root; UI at `:3000`, API at `:5000`

## Resource pipeline

`POST /api/resources` → `UrlIngestionJob` (metadata) → `AiAnalysisJob` (score/tags) → status `Inbox` or `Vault`.

Statuses (`ResourceStatus`): `New`, `Processing`, `AiAnalysing`, `Inbox`, `Vault`, `Archived`, `Trash`, `Error`.

## Key design

- TPT: `VideoResource`, `ArticleResource` extend `Resource`
- Separate `InboxMetadata` / `VaultMetadata` tables (not columns on Resource)
- All queries filtered by current user in `AppDbContext`
- AI: multiple `IAiProvider` beans from `Ai:Model_*` config, OpenRouter endpoint

## Frontend API

- All calls: `knowledgeos-frontend/lib/api.ts`
- Types: `lib/types.ts`
- `/api` proxied to backend via `next.config.ts` → `INTERNAL_API_URL`

